# Brief: pixel-art night sky

## What the input asks (quoted)
> 用图像生成模型生成一张 800×600 的像素风夜空背景 PNG（不要用代码画），提交到美术仓库的 assets/sky.png，并在仓库里写明它是怎样生成的。

## Focus and priorities
1. `assets/sky.png` exists in the artist repository: a real PNG, exactly 800x600, pixel-art night sky (stars, moon/gradient or similar), usable as a game background.
2. It must be produced by an image-generation model, not drawn with code (no PIL/canvas/numpy procedural drawing of the picture itself). Post-processing needed to meet size/format (resize/nearest-neighbour downscale, palette quantisation, PNG conversion) is allowed only if disclosed, and the content must come from the model.
3. The repository documents the generation: model name/version and how it was reached, exact prompt(s) and parameters, seed if any, raw output size, every post-processing step and its tool, date. Honest: if something is unknown, say so.

## Acceptance standard
- File at the path, valid PNG, 800x600 verified by running a check.
- Looks like pixel art and a night sky when viewed (I will open the image).
- Generation note present in the artist repo under `assets/` and consistent with how the file was really made; no code-drawn image.
- If no image-generation model is reachable, the artist must report that with evidence rather than substitute a code-drawn image.

## Not established
- Which image-generation model/endpoint is available in this world; the artist owns finding out.

## Split
Artist delivers `assets/` (sky.png + generation note). Producer: brief, assignment, acceptance. No build/quality/playtest positions; none are needed.
